 "about_text": "Art Share L.A. is a nonprofit arts organization in the Arts District of downtown Los Angeles, occupying a 30,000-square-foot building that combines 30 affordable artist lofts with exhibition and performance space. Its mission is to provide emerging artists equitable access and opportunity, connecting them to a supportive creative environment where they can live, work, develop, perform, and exhibit. The organization emphasizes diversity, equity, and inclusion, aiming to counter barriers faced by Black, Indigenous, People of Color, disabled, LGBTQ+, low-income, and other historically marginalized artists. It also advocates for fair, living wages for artists and staff, and works to connect artists with paid opportunities, from art sales to public art commissions.",
